    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new idempotency acceptance test.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe change is in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`).\n\nSince `addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` comes from the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface, I read the header without altering the generated signature:\n\n1. **Header read** \u2014 `currentIdempotencyKey()` pulls the `Idempotency-Key` header from the bound request via `RequestContextHolder`/`ServletRequestAttributes`, returning `null` when it's absent or blank.\n\n2. **Replay store** \u2014 a singleton-scoped `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> ownersByIdempotencyKey` maps each seen key to the id of the owner it created.\n\n3. **Short-circuit** \u2014 at the top of `addOwner`, if a key is present and already recorded, the original owner is re-fetched and returned with **200 OK** (mapped through the same `OwnerMapper`), skipping all creation/validation/duplicate logic.\n\n4. **Record on success** \u2014 after a successful `saveOwner`, the key\u2192id mapping is stored, and the first create still returns **201 CREATED** as before.\n\nBehavior matches the spec: a repeat create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with 200 instead of a duplicate (which would otherwise 409). Requests without the header are completely unaffected.",
