    "probe_text": "The controller source confirms the trace. Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Validations & side-effects, in order\n\n**Before the method body runs (framework layer):**\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise auth is disabled.)\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** \u2014 the request body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, so its constraints run before the handler: `@NotNull`/`@Size`/`@Pattern` on `firstName` & `lastName`, `@Size(max=10)` `title`, `@Size` on `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, `@NotNull @Size` `city`, `@NotNull @Size` `telephone`, `@Size` + `@Email` on `email`. Any failure \u2192 400.\n\n**Inside `addOwner` (in this exact sequence):**\n\n3. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, returns the previously created owner (**200 OK**) and skips everything below.\n4. `validateRequiredFields(dto)` \u2014 firstName, lastName, address (flat or line1), city, telephone must be non-blank \u2192 else **400**.\n5. `validatePostcode(postcode, city)` \u2014 if postcode present, must be 4 digits and within the city's regional range \u2192 else **400**.\n6. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` \u2014 **maps DTO \u2192 Owner** (id and pets ignored). *(side-effect: object construction)*\n7. `applyAddress(owner, dto)` \u2014 **normalizes/composes the address** (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE; prefers structured addressLine1 over the flat address); sets addressLine1/2 + composed address.\n8. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate(...)` \u2014 supplied registrationDate after today \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Default & normalize registration date** \u2014 null \u2192 today; then `toBusinessDay(...)` **rolls weekends/public holidays forward**, and the result is written back onto the owner.\n10. `rejectWhenDailyLimitReached(date)` \u2014 \u2265100 owners on that business day \u2192 **429**.\n11. `rejectWhenCityAtCapacity(city)` \u2014 \u226550 owners in that city \u2192 **409**.\n12. `applyHousehold(owner, sharesHousehold)` \u2014 computes a deterministic **householdId** (SHA-256 of lastName|postcode) and sets it; if that household already exists and `sharesHousehold` is not `true` \u2192 **409**.\n13. `normalizeTelephone(...)` \u2014 strips separators, assumes +61, drops leading 0, enforces E.164 (`+` then 8\u201315 digits, correct national length) \u2192 else **400**; **sets telephone**.\n14. `normalizeEmail(...)` \u2014 blank allowed; otherwise **lower-cases**, syntax-checks (**400**), and rejects disposable domains (**400**); **sets email**.\n15. `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` \u2014 identity key `telephone|email|householdId` matching a non-deleted owner \u2192 **409**.\n16. `customerCode(owner)` \u2014 computes `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duplicated with a `-n` suffix; **sets customerCode**.\n17. `membershipNumber(...)` \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<fiscalYY>`; **sets membershipNumber**.\n18. `countNamesakes(first, last)` \u2014 case-insensitive first+last match among existing owners; **sets namesakeCount**.\n19. `flagPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)` \u2014 soft match on lastName+postcode with a different phone; **sets possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf** (never when sharesHousehold).\n20. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 `@Transactional` \u2192 `em.persist` (new owner). **No JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist` etc.) exist, and the entity-level `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints on `Owner` are **not** re-validated here.\n21. **Store owner id** under the idempotency key (if a key was supplied).\n22. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` \u2014 computes derived read-only fields (salutation, displayName, initials, telephoneDisplay, membershipPoints/Level, checkDigit, locality, timezone, bulkSignupWarning, contactPreference, ageBand, fiscalYear, selfLink, etc.).\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 \u2026\")`.\n24. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- Many of these steps (customerCode, countNamesakes, duplicate/capacity/daily-limit checks, household, and several derived DTO fields) each independently call `findAllOwners()` and scan the full owner table \u2014 the create path re-queries all owners many times.\n- The **entity-level** Bean Validation on `Owner`/`Person` (`@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName/city, `@Pattern` telephone) is effectively dead code on this path \u2014 the DTO constraints and the controller's private validators are what actually enforce input rules.\n- Despite the `/api/owners` URL and the \"standard Spring Boot / conventional Spring MVC\" framing in CLAUDE.md, this handler is far from a conventional CRUD create: the bulk of the behavior is hand-rolled business logic (business-day rollover, capacity/daily limits, household hashing, customer/membership code generation, duplicate flagging) living in the controller rather than the service layer.\n\nI didn't change anything \u2014 this is read-only analysis."
